[node name="KillBox" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The kill box under the arena, and the one node that had to grow with the levels rather than gain a copy per level.\n\nRADIUS 62.0, WHICH IS THE OUTER WALL. Everything that walks in PANOPTICON walks on one of four surfaces -- three galleries and the guard's platform -- and 5 shafts are cut clean through all three decks, the outermost reaching r=59.5. The roof is at y=-2.0: the lowest structure in the arena bottoms out at y=8.0 and there is no walkable surface between them, so ONE roof answers a fall from ANY level. A prisoner who drops through a shaft on level three falls 29.0 m into it without touching a thing.\n\nIt is a trigger and nothing else: no collision of its own, monitorable off, and a mask of 1048577 (bit 0, the layer a living body is on, plus bit 20, MatchController.GHOST_HAZARD_LAYER) so a prisoner and a ghost are both seen falling in. The courtyard floor is inside it too, which is what makes the middle of the map a drop.\n\nWHAT IT DOES IS NOT DECIDED HERE. scripts/match/kill_volume.gd resolves whatever entered to a participant and hands it to MatchController.handle_fall() -- the same door the rifle and the red traps kill through."
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 62.0000
roof_depth_metres = 2.0000
depth_metres = 34.0000

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="KillBox"]
editor_description = "Deliberately empty. KillVolume._build_shape writes a CylinderShape3D over it on ready, from the exports on the parent."

[node name="StartEnd" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The start is on level one and the end is on level three, directly above it. That is the whole change in one sentence: a prisoner no longer finishes a few metres behind where they set off, they finish 27 m above it, level with the tower they are running at."

[node name="StartPad" type="CSGBox3D" parent="StartEnd"]
