[node name="Cover" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "Cover on all three levels, grouped by level, two radial bands per level at r=47 and r=57 -- one either side of the racing line, which is what a 16 m deck has room for.\n\nCOVER GETS SHORTER AS THE LEVELS RISE, AND THAT IS ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN TASTE. The shadow a box throws is set by how steeply the guard looks down on it. Level one sits 27.0 m under the eye, a 27 degree look; level three sits only 0.0 m under it, a -1 degree look. Give all three the same 3 m box and level three's shadows run three times as long as level one's, and the top of the arena becomes one continuous covered corridor -- a level the guard can see and can never shoot into, which is as dead as one they cannot see at all. Heights of 3.0 / 2.6 / 2.2 m hold the shadow behind a piece to roughly the same few metres on every level. All three are far above the 1.11 m jump, so none can be hopped."

[node name="Level1" type="Node3D" parent="Cover"]
editor_description = "Cover on level 1: 11 pieces, 6.0 x 3.0 x 1.5 m, faces tangential so each presents its full width to the tower. Rotated off the level below so a climb is not the same lap again."

